1. Write the schema: a caveat, ip_allowed, on group editors of a doc
2. Engineering edits doc:design from the office network only; bob gets a viewer link for three seconds
3. Alice's edit access depends on where the request comes from; her view access does not
   doc:design edit user:alice (no context)     -> conditional, missing client_ip
   doc:design edit user:alice from 10.1.2.3    -> allowed
   doc:design edit user:alice from 203.0.113.9 -> denied
   doc:design view user:alice from 203.0.113.9 -> allowed
4. Which docs can alice edit, without and with her address?
   {"resource_ids": [], "conditional": [{"id": "design", "missing": ["client_ip"]}]}
   {"resource_ids": ["design"], "conditional": null}
5. Who can edit doc:design?
   [{"subject": "user:alice", "conditional": true, "missing": ["client_ip"]}]
6. Read doc:design's relationships: the caveat with its stored context, and which ones expire
   doc:design#editor@group:eng#member with {"name": "ip_allowed", "context": {"allowed": "10.0.0.0/8"}}
   doc:design#parent@folder:root
   doc:design#viewer@user:bob (expires)
7. Bob's link, before and after it runs out
   doc:design view user:bob   (no context)     -> allowed
   the link has run out, but the newest revision was committed before that: a snapshot never changes
   doc:design view user:bob   (no context)     -> allowed
   the next write commits a revision after the expiry, and from there on bob is denied
   doc:design view user:bob   (no context)     -> denied
   viewers of doc:design: []
